rk_title", "Portrayal": "work_title"}, "work_summary": {"Work": "work_description"}, "work_format": {"Work": "medium_format"}, "work_genre": {"Work": "genre"}, "release_date": {"Work": "release_publication_date"}}}, "reasoning": "Identified recurring real-world concepts across all four tables and normalized them into minimal entity types: (1) Character (fictional entity) with optional creator/originator; (2) Work (book/film/series/video game) with description, medium/format, genre, and a single date field covering publication/release/first published; (3) Performer (actor/actress) with bio and demographic attributes; and (4) Portrayal as an associative entity capturing the many-to-many relationship between Character and Performer in the context of a specific Work (since the same character can be portrayed by different performers and a performer can portray multiple characters, sometimes across different works/franchises). Attributes were merged via semantic equivalence (e.g., description/summary/blurb; type/work_medium/work_format; publication_date/release_date/first_published_at) to minimize redundancy while preserving completeness. Source columns map directly into these integrated attributes; where a column participates in the relationship (portrayed_by and work title), it maps to Portrayal as well as its base entity."}, "time": 10.907226500101388}}